    "summary": "Lovelight fireworks, scorching Black Peter, tight early‑70 set",
    "blurb": "The show erupts with an incendiary Turn On Your Lovelight and a scorching Black Peter. Jerry’s vocal drawl and guitar shine on Dire Wolf and Lovelight while Pigpen fuels the energy with organ‑driven numbers. The band delivers crisp folk‑rock grooves that capture early‑70 Dead spirit.",
    "review": "On January 10, 1970 at Golden Hall in San Diego, the Grateful Dead served up a concise but high‑energy set that still feels fresh today. Highlights include an iconic Turn On Your Lovelight where Pigpen’s organ and harmonica blaze, a ferocious Black Peter that showcases Jerry’s gritty vocals and guitar, and a punchy China Cat Sunflower that earned praise for “fierce” playing. The rhythm section locks in tight—Phil’s loping bass underpins the folk‑rock vibe on Dire Wolf while Bob adds solid rhythmic texture—and Pigpen’s presence is felt throughout, especially on Good Lovin’ and the closing Lovelight romp. Though a few cuts run short and one reviewer called Mason's Children merely average, the overall performance is vibrant, with tight arrangements and plenty of raw Dead magic captured by several high‑quality soundboard sources.",
